{
  "assessment": "The source provides two quantitative inversion-rate formulas for the identical-ion and isotope-substituted clusters, but the isotope-substituted cluster lacks a reported numeric inversion rate formula over a shared alpha domain. The identical-ion cluster has a K-L rate formula with fitted temperature and background rate, and the isotope-substituted cluster has a reported activation barrier of ~270 mK at alpha ~1.09, but no rate formula. Thus, the hinted cluster is partially supported; case_authoring_ready is false because no numeric control domain is shared between the two branches.",
  "case_authoring_ready": false,
  "source": {
    "citation": "Akhil Ayyadevara, Symmetry-Controlled Thermal Activation in Pyramidal Coulomb Clusters: Testing Kramers-Langer Theory, Physical Review Letters (2026), DOI:10.1103/xsdn-srjd",
    "journal_doi": "10.1103/xsdn-srjd",
    "arxiv_versioned_id": "2601.04883v1"
  },
  "paper_scope": "The paper studies thermally activated inversion dynamics of five-ion Coulomb clusters in a Paul trap, comparing identical 40Ca+ ions (pseudo-rotation pathway) with isotope-substituted 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 (turnstile rotation pathway), testing Kramers-Langer theory against experiments and MD simulations.",
  "mechanisms": [
    {
      "mechanism_id": "kramers_langer_rate",
      "statement": "The multidimensional Kramers-Langer escape rate from a local minimum is given by kappa = N * (lambda^+ / 2pi) * sqrt(det U / |det U'|) * exp(-E_b / k_B T), where E_b is the energy barrier, U and U' are Hessians at equilibrium and saddle, lambda^+ is the positive eigenvalue of the dynamical matrix at the saddle, and N is the number of equivalent pathways.",
      "equations": [
        "kappa = N * (lambda^+ / (2*pi)) * sqrt(det(U) / |det(U')|) * exp(-E_b / (k_B * T))",
        "det(m * lambda^2 * I + gamma * lambda * I + U') = 0"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["kappa", "N", "lambda^+", "U", "U'", "E_b", "k_B", "T", "gamma", "m"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "N_identical",
          "value": 4,
          "uncertainty": "none",
          "unit": "dimensionless",
          "role": "number of equivalent pathways for identical-ion cluster",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 147,
              "line_end": 147,
              "support": "We also set N = 4 since the apex ion can replace any of the four base ions."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 137,
          "line_end": 145,
          "support": "The escape rate from a local minimum predicted by the multidimensional K-L theory is kappa = N (lambda^+ / 2pi) (det U / |det U'|)^{1/2} exp(-E_b / k_B T), with definitions of E_b, U, U', lambda^+, and N."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "pseudo_rotation_barrier",
      "statement": "For the identical-ion cluster, the pseudo-rotation pathway reduces the activation barrier by two orders of magnitude from ~1 K to ~20 mK, and the barrier decreases with lowering alpha.",
      "equations": [
        "E_b_pseudo_rotation ~ 20 mK (from ~1 K)"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["E_b"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "E_b_pseudo_rotation",
          "value": 0.02,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "K",
          "role": "activation barrier for pseudo-rotation pathway (identical ions)",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 448,
              "line_end": 448,
              "support": "This path relaxes to the Berry pseudo-rotation MEP, avoiding the high-energy center and reducing the activation barrier by two orders of magnitude (from ~1 K to ~20 mK)."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 448,
          "line_end": 448,
          "support": "The pseudo-rotation path reduces the activation barrier from ~1 K to ~20 mK."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 98,
          "line_end": 98,
          "support": "Lowering the trap aspect ratio alpha reduces the activation barrier, since it allows for a larger axial separation z0."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "mechanism_id": "turnstile_rotation_barrier",
      "statement": "For the isotope-substituted cluster (44Ca+ at apex), the turnstile rotation mechanism has an activation barrier of ~270 mK, which is significantly lower than umbrella inversion but high enough to suppress thermal activation at experimental temperatures.",
      "equations": [
        "E_b_turnstile_rotation ~ 270 mK"
      ],
      "variable_names": ["E_b"],
      "parameters": [
        {
          "name": "E_b_turnstile_rotation",
          "value": 0.27,
          "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
          "unit": "K",
          "role": "activation barrier for turnstile rotation pathway (isotope-substituted cluster)",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 450,
              "line_end": 450,
              "support": "The activation barrier is ~270 mK, which is significantly lower than the umbrella inversion but sufficiently high to suppress thermal activation at experimental temperatures."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 450,
          "line_end": 450,
          "support": "The cNEB optimization converges to a turnstile rotation mechanism with activation barrier ~270 mK."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "fixed_conditions": [
    {
      "condition_id": "identical_ions_alpha_1_09",
      "statement": "Identical-ion cluster (40Ca+)5 at trap aspect ratio alpha ~ 1.09, where rapid inversions are observed.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 111,
          "line_end": 111,
          "support": "Under identical trapping conditions (alpha ~ 1.09), the (40Ca+)5 cluster undergoes rapid inversions."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "isotope_substituted_alpha_1_09",
      "statement": "Isotope-substituted cluster 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 at trap aspect ratio alpha ~ 1.09, where inversions are suppressed.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 111,
          "line_end": 111,
          "support": "Under identical trapping conditions (alpha ~ 1.09), the 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 cluster remains locked in one orientation over long periods."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "identical_ions_alpha_range",
      "statement": "For identical ions, the bistable pyramidal configurations exist for 1.05 < alpha < 1.29.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 90,
          "line_end": 90,
          "support": "For 1.05 < alpha < 1.29, the global minima of V are two sets of inversion-broken square pyramids."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "isotope_substituted_alpha_range",
      "statement": "For the isotope-substituted cluster, the pyramid global minimum exists for alpha > ~1.35, and a local minimum with lighter isotope at apex exists only for alpha > 1.25.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 420,
          "line_end": 420,
          "support": "The pentagon global minimum transitions to a pyramid at alpha ~ 1.35, with the heavier isotope at the apex. A local minimum with lighter isotope at the pyramid apex only exists for alpha > 1.25."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "temperature_fitted",
      "statement": "Fitted cluster temperature T = 1.8 ± 0.1 mK from experimental inversion rates.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 151,
          "line_end": 151,
          "support": "The excess rate for alpha < alpha_th follows the K-L prediction over two orders of magnitude for a fitted temperature of T = 1.8 ± 0.1 mK."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "condition_id": "background_rate",
      "statement": "Background-gas collision rate R_bg = 0.10 ± 0.03 s^-1 for alpha > alpha_th ~ 1.1.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 151,
          "line_end": 151,
          "support": "For alpha > alpha_th, it saturates to R_bg = 0.10 ± 0.03 s^-1 due to background-gas collisions."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "controls": [
    {
      "name": "alpha",
      "definition": "Trap aspect ratio alpha = omega_z / omega_x, controlled by dc voltage on trap electrodes.",
      "unit": "dimensionless",
      "domain_kind": "continuous_interval",
      "minimum": 1.05,
      "maximum": 1.29,
      "allowed_values": [],
      "domain_statement": "For identical ions, bistable pyramidal configurations exist for 1.05 < alpha < 1.29.",
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 90,
          "line_end": 90,
          "support": "For 1.05 < alpha < 1.29, the global minima of V are two sets of inversion-broken square pyramids."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "readouts": [
    {
      "name": "inversion_rate",
      "definition": "Rate of thermally activated inversions between the two pyramidal configurations, extracted from exponential distribution of dwell times of the parity-odd octupole moment psi_30.",
      "unit": "s^-1",
      "statistic": "Exponential fit to dwell time histogram tail; for MD, from more than 2000 trajectories.",
      "uncertainty": "For experimental rates, uncertainty from exponential fits; for fitted temperature, ±0.1 mK; for background rate, ±0.03 s^-1.",
      "resolution": null,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 133,
          "line_end": 133,
          "support": "We extract the inversion rate kappa from an exponential distribution of the dwell time tau from more than 2000 trajectories."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 412,
          "line_end": 412,
          "support": "From the psi_30 time series, we bin the dwell times into a histogram and fit an exponential to the tail."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "activation_barrier",
      "definition": "Energy barrier E_b along the minimum energy path, computed via cNEB method.",
      "unit": "K",
      "statistic": "Computed from cNEB saddle point; energy difference between true saddle and cNEB maximum less than 1 microK.",
      "uncertainty": "source_unspecified",
      "resolution": null,
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 431,
          "line_end": 431,
          "support": "To identify the transition mechanisms and compute activation barriers, we employ the Climbing Image Nudged Elastic Band (cNEB) method."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 454,
          "line_end": 454,
          "support": "The energy difference between the true saddle point and the cNEB maximum is less than 1 microK."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "identical_ions_rate_kl",
      "statement": "For the identical-ion cluster, the experimentally measured inversion rate follows the Kramers-Langer prediction over two orders of magnitude for alpha < alpha_th ~ 1.1, with a fitted temperature T = 1.8 ± 0.1 mK and a background rate R_bg = 0.10 ± 0.03 s^-1 for alpha > alpha_th.",
      "quantitative_form": "kappa = N * (lambda^+ / (2*pi)) * sqrt(det(U)/|det(U')|) * exp(-E_b/(k_B*T)) with N=4, T=1.8e-3 K; for alpha > alpha_th, kappa = R_bg = 0.10 s^-1.",
      "mechanism_ids": ["kramers_langer_rate"],
      "control_names": ["alpha"],
      "control_domains": [
        {
          "control_name": "alpha",
          "domain_kind": "continuous_interval",
          "minimum": 1.05,
          "maximum": 1.29,
          "allowed_values": [],
          "domain_statement": "For identical ions, bistable pyramidal configurations exist for 1.05 < alpha < 1.29; the rate follows K-L for alpha < alpha_th ~ 1.1.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 90,
              "line_end": 90,
              "support": "For 1.05 < alpha < 1.29, the global minima of V are two sets of inversion-broken square pyramids."
            },
            {
              "line_start": 151,
              "line_end": 151,
              "support": "For alpha < alpha_th ~ 1.1, it grows rapidly as the barrier height is lowered, whereas for alpha > alpha_th, it saturates to R_bg."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "readout_names": ["inversion_rate"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["identical_ions_alpha_range", "temperature_fitted", "background_rate"],
      "applicability": "Applies to identical-ion (40Ca+)5 cluster in the bistable pyramidal regime 1.05 < alpha < 1.29, with temperature around 1.8 mK.",
      "statistical_basis": "Experimental rates from exponential fits to dwell time histograms; MD rates from more than 2000 trajectories; fitted temperature and background rate from experimental data.",
      "uncertainty": "Temperature uncertainty ±0.1 mK; background rate uncertainty ±0.03 s^-1; other uncertainties not specified.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 151,
          "line_end": 151,
          "support": "The excess rate for alpha < alpha_th follows the K-L prediction over two orders of magnitude for a fitted temperature of T = 1.8 ± 0.1 mK. For alpha > alpha_th, it saturates to R_bg = 0.10 ± 0.03 s^-1."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "isotope_substituted_suppression",
      "statement": "For the isotope-substituted cluster (44Ca+(40Ca+)4) at alpha ~ 1.09, thermally activated inversions are suppressed because the pseudo-rotation pathway is closed and the turnstile rotation has a high barrier of ~270 mK.",
      "quantitative_form": "E_b_turnstile = 270 mK; no rate formula reported.",
      "mechanism_ids": ["turnstile_rotation_barrier"],
      "control_names": ["alpha"],
      "control_domains": [
        {
          "control_name": "alpha",
          "domain_kind": "fixed_value",
          "minimum": null,
          "maximum": null,
          "allowed_values": [1.09],
          "domain_statement": "The suppression is observed at alpha ~ 1.09.",
          "anchors": [
            {
              "line_start": 111,
              "line_end": 111,
              "support": "Under identical trapping conditions (alpha ~ 1.09), the 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 cluster remains locked in one orientation over long periods."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "readout_names": ["activation_barrier"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["isotope_substituted_alpha_1_09"],
      "applicability": "Applies to isotope-substituted cluster with 44Ca+ at apex at alpha ~ 1.09.",
      "statistical_basis": "Activation barrier computed via cNEB; no rate measurement reported.",
      "uncertainty": "Barrier value ~270 mK with unspecified uncertainty.",
      "depends_on": [],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 111,
          "line_end": 111,
          "support": "The 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 cluster remains locked in one orientation over long periods, realizing a structural analog of a giant kinetic isotope effect."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 450,
          "line_end": 450,
          "support": "The activation barrier is ~270 mK, which is significantly lower than the umbrella inversion but sufficiently high to suppress thermal activation at experimental temperatures."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_ambiguities": [
    {
      "ambiguity_id": "alpha_domain_isotope",
      "statement": "The isotope-substituted cluster has a different alpha domain for pyramidal configurations (alpha > ~1.35 for global minimum) compared to the identical-ion cluster (1.05 < alpha < 1.29), and the suppression is observed at alpha ~ 1.09, which is outside the reported global minimum range for the isotope-substituted cluster. This may indicate a local minimum or metastable state.",
      "claim_ids": ["isotope_substituted_suppression"],
      "mechanism_ids": ["turnstile_rotation_barrier"],
      "control_names": ["alpha"],
      "readout_names": ["activation_barrier"],
      "fixed_condition_ids": ["isotope_substituted_alpha_1_09"],
      "anchors": [
        {
          "line_start": 420,
          "line_end": 420,
          "support": "The pentagon global minimum transitions to a pyramid at alpha ~ 1.35, with the heavier isotope at the apex. A local minimum with lighter isotope at the pyramid apex only exists for alpha > 1.25."
        },
        {
          "line_start": 111,
          "line_end": 111,
          "support": "Under identical trapping conditions (alpha ~ 1.09), the 44Ca+(40Ca+)4 cluster remains locked in one orientation."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
